syn_generic:|           |       |     | optimization.                                 |
syn_generic:|           |       |     |To also take dynamic power into account during |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | power optimization, set the                   |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' to a value     |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | between 0 and 1.                              |
syn_generic:|POPT-502   |Warning|    1|Total power has skewed contributions from      |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | leakage and dynamic power.                    |
syn_generic:|           |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified|
syn_generic:|           |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of  |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                     |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the      |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | design is not in the 'active period' but in   |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | 'idle mode', i.e. no dynamic power but only   |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | leakage power is consumed. For a reasonable   |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | optimization across dynamic and leakage power,|
syn_generic:|           |       |     | leakage contribution is expected to be above  |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | 5% and below 95%. A contribution of less than |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | 5% will result in limited leakage optimization|
syn_generic:|           |       |     | and contribution of more than 95% will result |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | in limited dynamic optimization. Adjust       |
syn_generic:|           |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage|
syn_generic:|           |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if|
syn_generic:|           |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.       |
