syn_generic:|DFT-220 |Info   |  144|Cannot unmap instance.                            |
syn_generic:|MAP-36  |Warning|    1|The floorplan checker finds some violations which |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | may impact quality of physical aware mapping or  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | structuring.                                     |
syn_generic:|        |       |     |Use 'check_floorplan -detailed' command to list   |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | the violation details and fix them if necessary. |
syn_generic:|POPT-502|Warning|    1|Total power has skewed contributions from leakage |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | and dynamic power.                               |
syn_generic:|        |       |     |Dynamic power is typically calculated/specified   |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | for some 'active period'. For combination of     |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | leakage and dynamic power                        |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio must specify the    |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | percentage of overall time for which the design  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | is not in the 'active period' but in 'idle mode',|
syn_generic:|        |       |     | i.e. no dynamic power but only leakage power is  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | consumed. For a reasonable optimization across   |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | dynamic and leakage power, leakage contribution  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | is expected to be above 5% and below 95%. A      |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | contribution of less than 5% will result in      |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | limited leakage optimization and contribution of |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | more than 95% will result in limited dynamic     |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | optimization. Adjust                             |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | 'opt_leakage_to_dynamic_ratio' so that leakage   |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | contribution comes to an intermediate value if   |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | you intend both optimizations to occur.          |
syn_generic:|ST-110  |Info   |    8|Connection established with super-threading       |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | server.                                          |
syn_generic:|        |       |     |The tool is entering super-threading mode and has |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | established a connection with a CPU server       |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | process.  This is enabled by the root attributes |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | 'super_thread_servers' or 'auto_super_thread'.   |
syn_generic:|ST-120  |Info   |    1|Attempting to launch a super-threading server.    |
syn_generic:|        |       |     |The tool is entering super-threading mode and is  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | launching a CPU server process.  This is enabled |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | by the root attribute 'super_thread_servers' or  |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | 'auto_super_thread'.                             |
syn_generic:|ST-128  |Info   |    2|Super thread servers are launched successfully.   |
syn_generic:|ST-136  |Warning|    1|Not obtained requested number of super thread     |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | servers.                                         |
syn_generic:|        |       |     |The requested number of cpus are not available on |
syn_generic:|        |       |     | machine.                                         |
