route:Applying the recommended capacitance filtering threshold values for 45nm process node: total_c_th=0, relative_c_th=1 and coupling_c_th=0.1.
route:	These values will be used by all post-route extraction engines, including TQuantus, IQuantus and Quantus QRC extraction.
route:	Capacitance filtering mode(extract_rc_cap_filter_mode option of the set_db) is 'relative_and_coupling' for all engines.
route:	The accuracy mode for post_route extract_rc_effort_level low extraction will be set to 'high'.
route:	Default value for EffortLevel(extract_rc_effort_level option of the set_db) in post_route extraction mode is 'medium'.
route:@flow 17: if {[get_feature -feature flow_express]} {...}
route:@@flow 20: set_db design_early_clock_flow              true
route:@flow 22: # Via naming
route:@flow 23: #-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
route:@flow 24: # Use design name as prefix for VIAs, as otherwise they will cause collision when merging designs on toplevel
route:@@flow 25: set_db write_stream_via_names true
route:@flow 27: # Timing attributes  [get_db -category timing && delaycalc]
route:@flow 28: #-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
route:@@flow 29: set_db timing_analysis_cppr           both
route:@@flow 30: set_db timing_analysis_type           ocv
route:@@flow 31: set_db timing_report_fields           {timing_point net cell fanout load transition delay incr_delay arrival edge user_derate power_domain}
route:@flow 33: #set_db timing_analysis_socv                               true                        ;# Enable socv analysis
route:@flow 34: #set_db timing_socv_rc_variation_mode                      true                        ;# Enable interconnect variation mode in SOCV mode
route:@flow 35: #set_db  timing_report_enable_verbose_ssta_mode true
route:@flow 37: # Add, TL: flow sets this to "no_async", async is default and should be used
route:@@flow 38: set_db timing_analysis_async_checks async
route:@flow 39: # Add, TL: maybe a bit hazardous... disable default io delay for ports which are unconstrained!
route:@flow 40: # if true, will cause hold problems (since launching clock is the receiving clock (with same latency!))
route:@@flow 41: set_db timing_apply_default_primary_input_assertion false
route:@@flow 43: set_db delaycal_advanced_node_pin_cap_settings true
route:@@flow 44: set_db delaycal_advanced_pin_cap_mode true
route:@flow 47: # Extraction attributes  [get_db -category extract_rc]
